{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>This is to me twenty years in your house.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): I served you with such great faithfulness, and you should have been mindful of my honor — all the more so since I am your son-in-law: I served you fourteen years for your two daughters and six years for your flocks, yet you did not deal so with me, for you changed my wages ten times." "<b>And the explanation of the matter</b> is that he changed them twice in every single year, and this is 'ten times' — that is, ten reckonings (עשרה מנינים). For he served him six years with the flock, and the first year stood as it was — that is, they were streaked, spotted, and speckled; but from the first year onward he changed it every single year twice: from streaked to spotted and from spotted to speckled, since small livestock give birth twice a year. And thus you have ten reckonings in five years." "<b>And by way of the Kabbalah:</b> זה לי עשרים שנה — like (Exodus 15:2): ״זה אלי ואנוהו״, and similarly (Exodus 13:8 — in some editions 13:14): ״בעבור זה עשה HaShem לי בצאתי ממצרים״. And since he already mentioned above, ״זה עשרים שנה אנכי עמך״, he should not have needed to repeat זה לי עשרים שנה בביתך. But the matter is that above he speaks of himself, whereas now he speaks of the Shekhinah, for HaShem, may He be exalted, was with him all twenty years that he was in his house. And from this he drew support for what follows: ״לולי אלהי אבי אלהי אברהם ופחד יצחק היה לי״ — and understand this."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:49.372248260Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}